+The orchestrator's text lists the agents, the repositories with the paths each protects in `.taik/protected`, and the products in `STATE/products`. A change to a listed product is a document. When the call of a named gate author fails, the service writes `STATE/crew/NAME.failed` with the error and removes it once that agent delivers a gate again. For six hours the agent is marked `(failed recently)`, and the orchestrator moves its gate to the first other agent that does not do the work. The standard worker is never marked.
+
 A reply to a finished job grants exactly one further round, and its worker reads the whole conversation. Each reply grants one round beyond the budget of four, at most eight. A worker may return a question instead of a candidate. Then nothing is judged, the question stands in the job, its cost in a record of its own, and the job waits until the user has answered. The viewer shows description, messages and rounds in the open ticket and plays a sound when a ticket starts to wait.
 
